<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>mboxer third-party licences</title>
<style>
  body { font: 15px/1.5 "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #1f2328; background: #fff; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #d0d7de; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f6f8fa; padding: 1rem; font-size: 13px; }
  ul.used-by { columns: 2; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #e6edf3; background: #0d1117; }
    h2 { border-color: #30363d; }
    pre { background: #161b22; }
    a { color: #58a6ff; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>
  mboxer compiles in the open-source Rust crates listed below, the ones of the platform this download is for
  (<code>mboxer.exe</code> on Windows, <code>mboxer.app</code> on macOS). Each licence text follows with the crates
  it covers and where their source is published; the crates are used unmodified. mboxer itself is released under
  the MIT licence: <a href="https://github.com/speti4/mboxer/blob/main/LICENSE">github.com/speti4/mboxer</a>.
  The web view is the operating system's own (Microsoft Edge WebView2 on Windows 11, WKWebView on macOS) and is
  not shipped with mboxer.
</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul class="used-by">
{{#each used_by}}
  <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
